WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.094 --> 00:00:05.062
The managers of the opera house had been agitated for some time. Awhile back they'd found

2
00:00:05.063 --> 00:00:13.551
a note from the ghost in their office, saying their first payment of twenty thousand francs

3
00:00:13.552 --> 00:00:18.050
was due. The ghost instructed them to put the money into the envelope he'd enclosed. They

4
00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:25.997
were told to seal it with wax before handing it to the usher Madame Giry to

5
00:00:25.998 --> 00:00:35.100
place in box five. Moncharmin and Richard did as they were told. Then they spent the

6
00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:39.467
evening watching the ghost's box to see who would pick up the envelope. When no one

7
00:00:39.468 --> 00:00:45.002
did, they went to the box and opened the envelope. Inside they found twenty thousand

8
00:00:45.003 --> 00:00:51.109
francs—but in play money! The seal on the envelope wasn't broken. So how had the money

9
00:00:52.001 --> 00:00:59.005
been replaced? Now, on the night when Christine was singing the role of Marguerite, it was

10
00:00:59.006 --> 00:01:03.821
time for another payment. The opera ghost had written, saying they should follow the same procedure.

11
00:01:03.822 --> 00:01:12.126
"I've sent for Madame Giry because she must know what's really going on with these payments,"

12
00:01:12.127 --> 00:01:20.905
Richard said to Moncharmin. The usher soon arrived at their office. "I assume you have another

13
00:01:20.906 --> 00:01:28.611
envelope for the ghost that you'd like me to deliver," she said. "Yes, and we want

14
00:01:28.612 --> 00:01:32.316
to talk to you about it." Richard picked up the envelope full of francs. "Anything at

15
00:01:32.317 --> 00:01:38.717
all, gentlemen," Madame Giry said. "We're not fools." Richard's expression hardened, and his voice grew harsh.

16
00:01:38.718 --> 00:01:47.322
"We know the opera ghost doesn't exist. You must be the accomplice of some con man.

17
00:01:47.323 --> 00:01:56.148
Tell us his name at once!" "I don't understand . . . an accomplice . .

18
00:01:57.438 --> 00:02:04.855
. what?" Madame Giry looked genuinely confused. "How much does this so-called ghost give you when

19
00:02:04.856 --> 00:02:09.872
you leave the envelope in his box?" Richard said. "Ten francs." "That's not much," Moncharmin said.

20
00:02:09.873 --> 00:02:14.521
"That's not all." Madame Giry hesitated before she spoke. "The ghost doesn't like me to talk

21
00:02:14.522 --> 00:02:21.863
about him, but awhile back he left me a letter in box five. In red

22
00:02:21.864 --> 00:02:29.235
ink he'd written a list of famous dancers and the years they'd married royalty. Next to

23
00:02:29.236 --> 00:02:39.096
a future year—1885—was my daughter Meg's name, followed by one word: empress!" Exhausted by her confession,

24
00:02:39.097 --> 00:02:48.746
Madame Giry flopped into a chair. "Before that letter I'd only half-believed in the opera ghost.

25
00:02:48.747 --> 00:02:56.662
After he declared that my Meg would one day marry the emperor, I totally believed in

26
00:02:56.663 --> 00:03:04.212
him." "You've never seen the ghost, yet you believe everything he says, no matter how improbable?"

27
00:03:05.059 --> 00:03:12.496
Moncharmin asked. "Yes! I told the ghost, if Meg's going to become empress, she'll need to

28
00:03:12.497 --> 00:03:20.032
attract the attention of the emperor. The phantom said something to the previous managers, and Meg

29
00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:27.960
immediately started getting better roles." Richard gave Moncharmin a skeptical look. "And now, madame, I'll tell

30
00:03:27.961 --> 00:03:33.041
you another reason I sent for you. I'm going to have you arrested for the theft

31
00:03:33.042 --> 00:03:44.309
of twenty thousand francs!" Madame Giry popped up from her chair and slapped Richard across the

32
00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:48.838
face. Shocked, he dropped the envelope, which opened, scattering the notes. "Look at all that money!"

33
00:03:48.839 --> 00:03:57.036
Madame Giry exclaimed. The managers dropped to the floor, quickly gathering up the notes. "I had

34
00:03:57.037 --> 00:04:04.917
no idea what was in that envelope!" Richard clutched the envelope tightly as he stood up.

35
00:04:06.247 --> 00:04:15.937
"What happened to the money we gave you last time?" "If anyone should know, it's

36
00:04:15.938 --> 00:04:20.170
you, Monsieur Richard!" Madame Giry said. "Because I put the envelope in the pocket of your

37
00:04:20.171 --> 00:04:26.544
coattail!" "What?" Richard made a move toward Madame Giry. "Here, let me take over," Moncharmin said,

38
00:04:26.545 --> 00:04:31.491
stepping between his partner and the usher. "Now please explain what you did with the envelope

39
00:04:31.492 --> 00:04:36.241
containing the real money." "I told you—I put it in Monsieur Richard's pocket. The one I

40
00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:45.069
left in box five was an identical envelope, which the ghost gave me beforehand and I

41
00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:51.888
slipped up my sleeve." At this point, Madame Giry took from her sleeve an envelope that

42
00:04:51.889 --> 00:04:59.459
matched the one Richard was holding. The managers turned the envelope over and saw it was

43
00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:06.052
sealed with wax stamped with their own seal. Upon opening it, they found twenty thousand francs

44
00:05:06.961 --> 00:05:12.556
in play money. "Amazing!" Moncharmin said. "How did he get our seal?" "Everyone's a magician these

45
00:05:12.557 --> 00:05:17.779
days!" Richard grumbled. "Why do you think the ghost went to all this trouble?" Moncharmin said.

46
00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:23.151
"He doesn't want anyone to see him picking up the envelope," Madame Giry said. "So after

47
00:05:23.152 --> 00:05:28.816
you gave me the one with the real money, I kept it up my sleeve. When

48
00:05:28.817 --> 00:05:34.601
I went to the ballet foyer to visit Meg, it was crowded as always, and easy

49
00:05:34.602 --> 00:05:44.274
for me to slip behind Monsieur Richard. That's when I put the envelope into the

50
00:05:44.275 --> 00:05:48.699
tail pocket of his coat." Richard rolled his eyes with disbelief. "You're lying! I spent that

51
00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:52.150
whole evening watching box five and the envelope you put there. I didn't go near the

52
00:05:52.151 --> 00:06:01.656
ballet foyer!" Madame Giry gave a satisfied smile. "I didn't give you the envelope that night.

53
00:06:02.461 --> 00:06:09.157
I waited until the next night when you were busy greeting the mayor." "Wait a minute!"

54
00:06:09.158 --> 00:06:14.608
Richard said. "I do remember you bumping against me. Was that when it happened?" Madame Giry

55
00:06:14.609 --> 00:06:24.005
nodded. "You didn't even know the real money was in your pocket. All the ghost had

56
00:06:24.006 --> 00:06:33.483
to do was come up behind you and take it." "Well, that's not going to happen

57
00:06:33.484 --> 00:06:39.511
tonight!" Richard called for the managers' assistant. "Mercier, come here! Lock Madame Giry in your office

58
00:06:39.512 --> 00:06:47.820
so she can't communicate with her ghost friend." Mercier escorted the protesting usher away while the

59
00:06:47.821 --> 00:06:55.062
managers discussed what to do. "We need to get to the bottom of this mystery," Moncharmin

60
00:06:55.063 --> 00:06:59.651
said. "For now, the safest thing to do is lock ourselves in the office until after

61
00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:07.595
the performance." Richard nodded. "When Mercier returns," Moncharmin went on, "let's ask him for a safety

62
00:07:08.788 --> 00:07:19.324
pin to fasten the envelope—and the money—to your pocket. If the ghost tries to remove the

63
00:07:19.325 --> 00:07:24.910
envelope, you'll feel his hand in your pocket!" The managers were in their office all

64
00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:31.916
evening, so they were unaware of Christine's dramatic disappearance. Before they left for the night, Richard

65
00:07:31.917 --> 00:07:38.183
felt his pocket to be sure the money was still there. "I can feel the safety

66
00:07:38.184 --> 00:07:48.803
pin, but the envelope's gone!" Richard tore off his coat and turned his pocket inside out.

67
00:07:48.804 --> 00:07:57.271
It was empty! Moncharmin gasped. "The ghost must have been here!" "We would have seen him!"

68
00:07:57.272 --> 00:08:03.115
Richard said. At that moment Mercier knocked on the office door, shouting something about Christine. But

69
00:08:03.116 --> 00:08:10.953
the managers were too distraught about their twenty thousand francs to comprehend what he was saying.

